/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  flash12_nh3_acetic_ethanol_reactive -- the weak base MEETS the weak acid,
  with a molecular co-volatile watching: the ThermoResolver's reference case.

  Four apparent components, one liquid: ammonia (pKa 9.25) neutralises half
  of the acetic acid (pKa 4.76) into AMMONIUM ACETATE -- a buffer forms and
  the solved pH lands near pKa_HAc.  Ethanol carries the curated fact
  `aqueousSpeciation none;` -- the classifier finds it molecular and
  nonionising FROM THE RECORD (no case list, no name special-casing), the
  recommended mixed-solvent model is announced unavailable, and its ideal
  molecular VLE is explicitly AUTHORISED by the delimited approximations
  block.  Everything announced; the unauthorised path refuses by name.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

application   choupoSolve;
description  "Reactive 4-component flash: NH3 + HAc neutralise into an ammonium-acetate buffer (pH ~ pKa_HAc); ethanol classified nonionising from its record fact, ideal VLE authorised; subsaturated at 358.15 K";
verbosity     3;

reports
{
    streamTable    { }
    massBalance    { }
}
